  "id": "ambivalent-sexism",
  "term": "ambivalent sexism",
  "definition": "Ambivalent sexism is a form of sexism that combines openly negative views of women with seemingly positive attitudes that still place women below men. It includes both hostile reactions toward women and protective or idealizing attitudes that help justify male dominance.",
